    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "John Bowen, San Antonio’s first Anglo‑American postmaster, named the town after his friend John Pleasants.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pleasanton%2C_Texas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "In 1912 the Missouri Pacific Railroad linked Pleasanton to San Antonio, and by 1914 it was connected to Corpus Christi.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        12
